<title>GERMANY: German March M3 up annualised 8.3 pct vs 9.1 pct.</title>
<headline>German March M3 up annualised 8.3 pct vs 9.1 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bundesbank gave the following data for German M3 money supply growth in March.</p>
<p>						 March 97	   Feb 97</p>
<p> Annualised vs average Q4 1996	    8.3		  9.1 pct</p>
<p> Annualised vs average Q4 1995	    8.1		  8.3 pct</p>
<p> Non-annualised vs average Q4 1996	2.7		  2.2 pct</p>
<p>Note - The Bundesbank's target range for 1997 M3 money supply growth is 3-1/2 to 6-1/2 percent. Economists polled by Reuters predicted a slowdown in the annualised growth rate to about 8.3 percent versus the final quarter of 1996.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
